   "ec": "none",
   "ecWhy": "In EC the window becomes a range for a time variable, so an early start causes no problem (`research/calculi.md`, §4).",
   "summary": "In Req 10, $\\mathit{MkIntervalOO}(\\mathit{Now} - 10, \\mathit{Now})$ starts outside the time set when $\\mathit{Now} < 10$.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "title": "Explanation",
     "body": "$T = \\mathbb{R}_{\\ge 0}$, so $\\mathit{Now} - 10$ is not a time point for $\\mathit{Now} < 10$. The count is still right, because nothing happens before time 0, but the interval is not well-formed.\n\nA plain guard $\\mathit{Now} \\ge 10$ would be wrong: it would ignore TC2's failures at 0 s and 9 s. Clamping the open start to 0 would be wrong too, because it would exclude the failure at 0 s."
    },
    {
     "title": "Proposed fix",
     "body": "Use $[0, \\mathit{Now})$ when $\\mathit{Now} < 10$, and $(\\mathit{Now} - 10, \\mathit{Now})$ otherwise."
    }
   ],
