   "id": "receive-content",
   "kind": "problem",
   "title": "receive does not fix what is received",
   "short": "",
   "order": 0,
   "parent": "channel-design",
   "status": "open",
   "severity": "major",
   "found": "2026-10-04",
   "related": [
    "channel-design",
    "only-if-gap",
    "example-assertion-weak"
   ],
   "causedBy": [],
   "solves": [],
   "partlySolves": [],
   "needs": [],
   "alternativeTo": [],
   "ec": "blocker",
   "ecWhy": "A test's `receive` carries no value, so it cannot become the event $\\mathit{receive}(c, v)$ that Req 08's tests need.",
   "summary": "`receive(t, c, dst)` has no argument for the message's content, so a test that delivers a message cannot say what it contains.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "title": "Explanation",
     "body": "`receive` copies the channel's *current* value into a Signal `dst`; only `transmit` puts a value on a channel. A test describes an incoming message with one stimulus, so the content is left open.\n\n**Example (Req 08).** \"TC1: the software receives a MastershipInfo message at 1 s\":\n\n| Trace | Value on `MastershipInfo` at 1 s | Condition of Req 08 | Exercised? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| A | `BACKUP` | true | yes |\n| B | `PRIMARY` | false | no |\n\nThe checker cannot decide whether TC1 exercises Req 08."
    },
    {
     "title": "Proposed fix",
     "body": "Both channel designs give the message stimulus a value, $\\mathit{receive}(t, c, v)$. TC1 can then not be written without stating the content."
    }
   ],
   "affects": [
    {
     "req": "Req 08",
     "test": "",
     "note": "a test cannot state what was received"
    },
    {
     "req": "Req 08",
     "test": "TC1",
     "note": "the example test in `research/findings.md`"
    }
   ],
   "sources": "- `research/findings.md`, \"`receive` does not fix what is received\"",
   "file": "problems/items/receive-content.md"
