   "summary": "`formalism.tex` says a test case \"produces a concrete trace\", but its setup and stimuli fix only some values, so a test case allows many traces.",
   "sections": [
    {
     "title": "Explanation",
     "body": "The setup fixes values at time 0, and each stimulus fixes the values its effect predicate talks about. Everything else is left open, in particular everything the software does.\n\n**Example (Req 10, TC2).** The stimuli are two sensor failures, at 0 s and at 9 s. Nothing in the test says what `emergency_mode` does, so the test allows traces where it becomes true at 9 s, at 20 s, or never.\n\nA test case therefore stands for a **set of traces**:\n\n$$\\mathit{Traces}(\\mathit{TC}) = \\{\\, \\rho \\in \\Sigma^T \\mid \\rho(0) \\text{ agrees with } \\sigma_0, \\text{ and the effect of every stimulus holds in } \\rho \\,\\}$$\n\nThe assertions then say which of these traces the test expects."
    },
    {
     "title": "Fix",
     "body": "Replace \"to produce a concrete trace\" (Section \"Requirements & Test cases\" of `formalism.tex`) with the set-of-traces definition, and define the coverage checker over this set."
    }
   ],
